No -- firstly because "le broda" points to a specific thing, but not necess=
arily to an actual broda, hence its equivalence to "lo co'e voi broda", whe=
re co'e gives the specificity and voi gives the nonveridicality (the not ne=
cessarily actually being broda); and secondly because in the types-only mod=
el, everything that is an actual broda is a type.

But one can be hopeful that Martin can outline for lVi an instance-only sem=
antics, which perhaps the BPFK might consider.

